All of that is fake news, I'm sorry.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:16.010
The alcohol inhalation

00:04:16.010 --> 00:04:19.320
for nausea, actually has some evidence.

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.650
I looked it up, found
out it's actually true.

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:23.760
They used actually, non-pregnant patients

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:26.000
in an emergency room setting that had mild

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.130
to moderate nausea

00:04:27.130 --> 00:04:30.300
and they had them sniff
alcohol one to two centimeters

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.210
below their nose.

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:33.960
And half an hour later, 50% improved.

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:35.230
And obviously, there
were different studies

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:36.063
with different outcomes,

00:04:36.063 --> 00:04:38.310
But it seems like a really simple way

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:40.710
with low chance of adverse effects to try

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:43.000
and treat someone's nausea
without using medications.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.240
Because the most commonly
used medication that we have

00:04:45.240 --> 00:04:47.510
for nausea is called Ondansetron,

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.940
and it actually has serious
complications if it's used

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:50.920
in the wrong patient.

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:53.160
Meaning that if you already
have some cardiac arrhythmia,

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.090
it can make it become worse so much so,

00:04:55.090 --> 00:04:55.960
that it could be fatal.

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.350
And again, that shouldn't scare you away

00:04:57.350 --> 00:04:58.440
from taking that medication

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:00.910
if you're truly having
terrible nausea and vomiting.

00:05:00.910 --> 00:05:02.150
It's just a known side effect.

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:03.630
Sniffing a little alcohol,

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:05.500
literally smelling it
one to two centimeters

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:07.890
of your nose, very low chance
of adverse side effects

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:08.750
in my opinion.

